A delete below a root that asks for an interrupt before its first step
may stop having made no child a root,
and the call it stops starts again from where it began, as often as an interrupt is pending.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call was preempted before it took anything away
Witness: fuzz delete-root-makes-nothing

diff --git a/kernel/cap.c b/kernel/cap.c
--- a/kernel/cap.c
+++ b/kernel/cap.c
@@ -293,6 +293,9 @@ bool cap_delete(struct cap *n, bool preempt)
     }
     while (cap_child(n) != 0) {
         LOOP_PAID(cap_delete, link, "a child below a root, which becomes a root itself");
+        if (cap_stop_here(preempt)) {
+            return false;
+        }
         struct cap *c = node(cap_child(n));
         detach(c, false);
         cap_set_next(c, LINK_UP);
